  pages = {588--598},
  abstract = {The numbers of all three species of seals living in the Baltic Sea (Halichoerus grypus, Pusa hispida, Phoca vitulina) have considerably decreased during last decades. The analysis fo the history of the seal hunting and of some biological features of these species together with the analysis of environmental changes have revealed the reason the seal numbers reduction happened: sharp disturbance of the reproduction tale as a result of environmental anthropogenic pollution. Prospective tendencies of Baltic seals investigations are discussed.},
