  pages = {555--563},
  abstract = {The sloughed skin from three captive manatees at Lowry Park Zoological Garden (Tampa, Florida) was examined over a period of one year to determine its stable carbon isotopic composition ( *13C). The food *consumed by these manatees in a controlled diet was also sampled and its *13C values determined. The sloughed skin *13C values from the captive manatees were enriched by an average of +4.1\textperthousand{} relative to lettuce (generally \textquestiondown 98\% of the diet) the animals consumed. *13C values of the skin were shown to be related to changes in *13C values of the lettuce.},
