  abstract = {The somatic chromosomes of 2 beaked whales, M. europaeus and M. carlhubbsi and a balenopterid whale B. acutorostrata, were studied. The chromosome number of the beaked whales is 2n = 42. The karyotypes are morphologically similar. Both species have a large X chromosome due to accumulation of C-heterochromatin. The karyotype of B. acutorostrata is in good agreement with the general 2n = 44 cetacean karyotype. The 2n = 42 beaked whale karyotypes may have evolved from the general 2n = 44 karyotype through a fusion of 2 pairs.},
