  author = {Condy, P R},
  year = {1976},
  volume = {Research},
  pages = {2--8},
  abstract = {The census was carried out in Jan. and Feb. 1976. An area of 193 km2 was surveyed. The population density of crabeater seals Lobodon carcinophagus and leopard seals Hydrurga leptonyx compared well with the results of other workers and the 2 previous censuses in the King Haakon VII Sea. The density of Ross seals Ommatophoca rossi compared well with the results of the 2 previous surveys. The percentage species composition of the sample reflected the density relationship. Crabeater and Ross seals occurred in largest numbers on ice floes in the time period of 06:00-18:00, with a peak haul-out period of 08:00-14:00. Weddell seals were most commonly observed at 14:00-16:00, and leopard seals were only seen at 04:00-18:00.},
