  abstract = {In Juli 1990, a Morbillivirus epidemic decimated the striped dolphin (Stenella coeruleoalba) population in the Mediterranean sea. The epidemic started in Spain and advanced progressively to the shores of Turkey. The article describes the chronology oi the phenomenon, the symptoms and lesions observed, and summarises curent Knowledge concerning the Morbillivirus responsible for these deaths. The environmental factors (pesticide and heavy metal pollution, and trophic factors) which favour the disease are highlighted as well as the consequences on marine mammal population in the Mediterranean sea.},
