  abstract = {A male specimen of Miroungo leonina Linnaeus, 1758 age estimated between 7-8 years old, collected at Santa Vitoria do Palmar, Rio Grande do Sul State, southernmost Brazil (32degree44'S and 53degree22'W) is presented. All the Skeleton was recovered except the rostral region. It shows an advanced osteomyelitis in the left dentary, extending from the synfisis until the middle portion of the body; as well as Scheuermann disease at lumbar vertebrae. Such diseases could explain its presence at that locality, when it was shot. The bullet was recovered from the rostrum, and might be responsible for death. This is the first virtually complete skeleton of M. leonina recovered from Brazilian coast.},
