  abstract = {30. HOUSE CAT Felis catus Linnaeus, 1758 Distribution Feral cats were reported as eradicated by ground shooting from Motuihe Island in the Hauraki Gulf sometime during or before 1981 (Veitch \& Bell 1990), but are still present on the island (S. Mowbray, Department of Conservation (DOC) Auckland Area Office pers.comm.). It is unknown if the cat population has recovered (S. Mowbray pers.comm.) or if they were re-introduced to the island (Veitch 1991). Feral cats were never very abundant on Campbell Island (Dilks 1979) and are now believed to be extinct there, since extensive searches of the island by DOC staff using trained dogs in January and August 1999 found none (I. McFadden DOC Biodiversity Recovery Unit, Wellington pers.comm.).},
